const representation="Use the actual complex Lie algebra LR.L=LieAlgebra.SpecialLinear.sl (Fin 2) ℂ, the subtype of trace-zero 2×2 matrices with commutator bracket (pinned Classical.lean:94–99). x,y,h remain arbitrary Chevalley generators: H002 explicitly records IsSl2Triple h x y, their complex linear span being all of LR.L, the Lie representation law, finite dimension λ+1, irreducibility and existence of a primitive highest-weight vector. The pinned IsSl2Triple declaration includes h≠0 and exactly [x,y]=h, [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, where 2• is natural repeated addition. A linear rho plus its explicit H002 commutator law is the usual Lie representation, avoiding an implicit theorem in a typeclass. H003 retains the chosen nonzero highest-weight vector. H001 keeps primality, CharP, nonnegativity and the strict λ<p bound as propositions, not parameter capabilities. K has only Field as structural data, with no algebraic-closure assumption.\nThe integer λ is retained. I=Fin(λ.toNat+1) uses values 0,...,λ.toNat; H001 gives λ.toNat=λ under the natural/integer inclusion, so this is exactly the source integer interval. Fin.last λ.toNat is the source index λ, not an ordering by an unrelated enumeration. Natural subtraction is used only under the displayed index/branch inequalities. Nat.choose uses natural top and lower indices and is cast into ℂ/R/K; its factorial formula applies under precisely those bounds. Endomorphism multiplication is right-to-left composition, verified in the pinned Module.End.mul_apply; powers at exponent zero are identities.\nM is a Submodule ℤ V, equivalently the source additive subgroup. H004 states existence of simultaneous integer/complex bases with the same underlying vectors, with no preselected standard lattice, and preservation by every divided power. This is equivalent to preservation by the unital integer subalgebra U_Z: one direction uses its generators; the other uses closure under integers, sums, products and identity. Only the image of U_Z in Endℂ(V) acts, so no faithfulness of the enveloping-algebra action is assumed. dp f r=(r! : ℂ)⁻¹ • f^r and eNat=dp y i v are actual definitions, not hypotheses about their actions.\nR is the subring closure in ℚ of the explicitly displayed p-free-denominator fractions. T006 proves that this closure is exactly that set, rather than assuming localization facts in a definition. MR=R⊗ℤM. Its inclusion into V is represented by an existential ℤ-linear f with the exact pure-tensor formula and an explicit R-scalar compatibility law; no embedding is a parameter. Coefficient modules use the required R-action on C=RestrictScalars R ℚ ℂ. The pinned RestrictScalars.module and smul_def use the actual subtype inclusion R→ℚ and the ordinary rational action on ℂ; cv is the supplied additive equivalence C≃+ℂ, and T011 checks its scalar formula before use. Statements of membership, generated submodules and sums explicitly cross cv, rather than guessing coercions. The J in N003 is characterized at every index, hence is the source J0 and all Ji; finite products over I represent the finite direct sum.\nVK is K⊗ℤM, identified with the source M⊗ℤK by the standard tensor flip, preserving the K-action on the scalar factor. Likewise LK is K⊗ℤ(spanℤ{x,y,h}), not a trace-zero-matrix algebra over K. Action is a result structure, produced in T007/N002, not an input assumption. It records the restricted integer action, bracket closure, and a K-linear map whose exact pure-tensor formula and pure-tensor commutator identity give the Lie action by multilinearity; a,d,t are exactly its three generator actions. Lift characterizes the unique reduced operator through an actual integer-linear restriction and its pure-tensor formula. There are no defaults or arbitrary selected operators.\nResidue is also produced, not assumed. Its maps specify fractions, the canonical ZMod p→K inclusion, kernel pR and quotient ring isomorphism. Each occurrence of the scalar-extension tensor K⊗R MR uses exactly phi.toAlgebr